+# Add t and use it to validate PlaceBlock arguments
+
+## What
+
+- Adds the [t](https://github.com/osyrisrblx/t) runtime type checker (`osyrisrblx/t`, pinned to `=3.1.1`, the latest
+  version on the Wally index) to `pesde.toml`, pulled from Wally through pesde like our other packages. It mounts at
+  `ReplicatedStorage.Packages.t`.
+- Switches the `PlaceBlock` handler in `src/ServerScriptService/BlockPlacement.server.luau` from hand-written
+  `typeof` checks to a `t.tuple` checker, so later remotes can follow the same pattern.
+- Lists t in the README's package table.
+
+## Checks kept
+
+All argument checks the handler made before still happen, in the same order, and a failing check still drops the
+request silently:
+
+| Before | After |
+|---|---|
+| `typeof(blockTypeName) == "string"` | `t.string` |
+| `typeof(position) == "Vector3"` | `t.Vector3` |
+| `position == position` (reject NaN components) | `isNotNaN`, combined with `t.Vector3` through `t.intersection` (t has no NaN check) |
+
+The game-rule checks after that (known block type, rate limit, character present, cell above ground and free, within
+reach) are unchanged.
+
+## Before testing
+
+**`pesde.lock` is not updated in this PR.** Installs couldn't be run where this change was written, so the lockfile
+has no entry for t yet. Before testing or merging:
+
+1. From the project root, run `pesde install`. This resolves t, updates `pesde.lock`, and creates
+   `roblox_packages/t`.
+2. Commit the updated `pesde.lock` to this branch.
+3. Regenerate the sourcemap so luau-lsp sees the new package, then run the usual checks:
+
+   ```sh
+   rojo sourcemap default.project.json -o sourcemap.json --include-non-scripts
+   luau-lsp analyze --platform=roblox --definitions:@roblox=globalTypes.d.luau --sourcemap=sourcemap.json --ignore=**/roblox_packages/** src
+   selene src
+   stylua --check src
+   ```
+
+   None of these were run for this change, so please treat the results as the first check.
+
+Without step 1, `require(ReplicatedStorage.Packages.t)` fails and the whole `BlockPlacement` script errors at load,
+so no blocks can be placed.
+
+## How to test
+
+In Studio after `rojo serve`, from a client (e.g. the command bar in client context):
+
+- `ReplicatedStorage.PlaceBlock:FireServer(<valid block name>, Vector3.new(0, 4, 0))` near the spawn places a block.
+- Each of these places nothing and raises no server error:
+  - a non-string block name, e.g. `FireServer(123, Vector3.new(0, 4, 0))`
+  - a non-Vector3 position, e.g. `FireServer(<name>, CFrame.new())` or `FireServer(<name>, nil)`
+  - a NaN position, e.g. `FireServer(<name>, Vector3.new(0/0, 4, 0))`
+  - an unknown block name
